
What is TreeMap?
  - It is Implemented class of Navigable map but it also inherits properties of sortedMap And Map Interface.

Syntax:
     package java.util;
    class TreeMap implement NavigableMap,clonable,serializable{
        //constructors
        //methods
    }

  - it was introduced in JDK 1.2 version.
  - Treemap underline data Structure is "Red-Black Tree".


PROPERTIES OF TREEMAP
   - we store the data in key value pair in which key should be unique values can be duplicate.
   - Treemap does not follow the insertion order but follow the sorting order with respect to keys.
   - It can store homogenous and hetrogenous elements.
   - TreeMap cannot Store Null value.
   - TreeMap Non Syncronized data structure.

PROPERTIES OF RED-BLACK TREE

   -Every Node Either red or black color.
   -The root node is always black.
   -Every leaf node is black.
   -If a node is red,then both its children are black.
